    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418-a1">

                <pb facs="0621" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg527"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 282.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs,<lb/>Department of Interior
                                Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                            Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27/April 8,
                            1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Referring to the notes of the
                    legation of the United States of America of December 8/20, 1895, and February
                    6/18 of the current year, relating to Henry Topor, I have the honor to transmit
                    to you herewith an extract from a document of the department of medicine
                    containing the facts regarding the arrest and the present condition of the
                    above-named person.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chichkine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
